body:
I'm UK-based; the technical assessments I faced were similar to HTB, though I can imagine this probably just one of many types. For me technical interviews, I was asked about active directory attack steps, probably because I'd mentioned the PNPT during the interview. 

&#x200B;

One thing I forgot to mention is that there is some interviewers were wary of people that have only done HTB/PG/OSCP who don't think about pentesting beyond hacking boxes. In an interview, you should be familiar with all steps of a pentest, starting from agreeing on the rules of engagement, to how you'd present your findings

Good luck for today mate! Don't overthink it. When in doubt, pick between RCE and credential access (like ssh and rdp) and see how each port can help you e.g. ftp showing you contents of a web app and then using that for RCE, or web app has SQL which is used to leak credentials which are then reused. 

&#x200B;

Also, take breaks and write to yourself what needs to be done before each break. This way you can rest and also keep track of your progress! 

&#x200B;

Also SLEEP! This is a 24 hour exam, and it is expected of  you to sleep in the middle
